= The London Ultimatum

On 5 May the Allies send Berlin their bill for the war: 132 billion gold marks, paid in instalments, with a demand for acceptance within six days. If Germany refuses, the Ruhr will be occupied. French troops already hold Düsseldorf, Duisburg and Ruhrort since March.

[? if e21_new_cabinet = 1 : Fehrenbach's cabinet has already resigned. On 10 May Joseph Wirth of the Centre forms a new government with the SPD and the DDP and accepts the ultimatum. The Reichstag votes yes, 220 to 172. Wirth calls it the policy of fulfilment: pay, and show the world that it cannot be paid. ?][? if kapp_outcome = 3 : The workers' government must answer the ultimatum. Its ministers accept it, with a promise that the rich will pay, and every party to our right accuses them of treason. ?][? if kapp_outcome = 2 : The generals' government blusters, then accepts. There is no Reichstag vote worth the name. ?]

Who will pay? The printing presses of the Reichsbank are already running.

- @against: Vote against: the workers will pay for it.
- @real_values: Demand that the rich pay: seize real values.
- @versailles: Denounce Versailles and the Entente.

@against
subtitle: The Left's line. Clear and simple, and it changes nothing.
on-arrival: offensive_satisfaction += 4; militancy += 2; lean_offensive += 1

Our deputies vote no. The Rote Fahne prints a cartoon of Wirth handing over a worker's wage packet to a French general.

@real_values
subtitle: The Right's line: a demand the unions can take up, and the start of a programme.
on-arrival: worker_support += 3; uspd_relation += 3; unionist_satisfaction += 6; lean_unionist += 2

The party demands the seizure of real values: a fifth of the shares, land and buildings of the propertied classes, to pay the reparations instead of the printing press. The demand is taken up at union meetings in Saxony and Thuringia.

@versailles
subtitle: A popular note, but it brings us close to the nationalists.
on-arrival: worker_support += 1; independence += 2; luxemburgist_satisfaction -= 4; offensive_satisfaction += 2; lean_offensive += 1

The Rote Fahne calls the ultimatum the enslavement of the German people. The nationalist press quotes us approvingly. Zetkin is furious.
